+++ b/docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats-roast-design-1-step-back.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+decision: local
+triggers: shared-cause, defect-type
+summary: No redesign. The 10 r1 findings form three clusters, each one rule applied unevenly (exit-code classification in §4.4, the no-IPC_VERSION-bump compatibility rule in §4.1/§4.12, and node-manager permanence in §4.7/§4.9), plus two independent nits. Sweep each cluster with one rule rather than patching per finding.
+pattern: Two decisions are each stated as a list of specific cases instead of the rule behind them, so the roast found the cases the list missed. (1) §4.4 cli::daemon_error maps ClientError variants by type instead of by condition, so Frame, Remote{Unavailable} and the NoEnsure "not in Herdr" case fall through (r1 [Should-fix] §4.4 / Key abstractions cli::daemon_error "anything else → the error, exit 1", r1 [Should-fix] §4.4 / cli::daemon_error closed mapping, r1 [Nit] §4.4 'Not being inside a Herdr pane ...'). The §4.1 no-bump decision has the same shape: it has no wire-compatibility rule (r1 [Nit] §4.1 ..., r1 [Nit] §4.12 'WhoReply gains manager_chain ...'). (2) §4.9 states node-manager permanence as per-path exemptions (seat and clones excluded from cascade, move "restored", designation only checks "live") instead of one invariant that every path is checked against (r1 [Should-fix] §4.9 Observation bullet ..., r1 [Should-fix] §4.9 'An observed move ...', r1 [Nit] §4.7 'Target must exist and be live' ...). Both are fixable inside their own sections. Neither needs another decision changed, and the Goal and Requirement baseline (B2, B8, B11) already fix the intent.
+clusters:
+- C1-exit-classification: r1 [Should-fix] §4.4 / Key abstractions cli::daemon_error "anything else → the error, exit 1", r1 [Should-fix] §4.4 / cli::daemon_error closed mapping, r1 [Nit] §4.4 'Not being inside a Herdr pane (HERDR_SOCKET_PATH unset) is not a daemon outage: it gets its own variant ... never the retry-later text' | rule: cli::daemon_error classifies by condition, not by ClientError variant, and the mapping must be complete over every ClientError variant and IpcErrorCode. The helper checks HERDR_SOCKET_PATH itself, for every CallMode, before anything else (exit 2, no retry text). Any failure to get a well-formed reply from a working daemon goes to exit 5: Unavailable, Frame (I/O, timeout, truncated or undecodable frame) and Remote{code: Unavailable}. State explicitly whether VersionMismatch joins exit 5. Remote{Integrity} goes to exit 6. NoInstance goes to exit 2. Command-specific Remote arms are handled before the helper. Everything else is exit 1. §4.14 / hg-k4l.2 tests cover one row per variant or code, including a hung daemon and a daemon that is still starting.
+- C2-wire-compat-without-version-bump: r1 [Nit] §4.1 'A stale daemon paired with a new CLI can at worst produce a frame error instead of a message', r1 [Nit] §4.12 'WhoReply gains manager_chain: Vec<{seat, name}>'; §4.1 'without bumping IPC_VERSION' | rule: §4.1 states one compatibility rule for the no-bump decision and names both skewed pairs. Every new reply or record field is #[serde(default)] (manager_chain, reports, manager, node_manager, threads_seat), so new CLI + old daemon parses. The new IpcErrorCode::Integrity is accepted as a new-daemon + old-CLI degradation to a frame error, which C1 routes to exit 5 (or the spec adds a #[serde(other)] catch-all and says so).
+- C3-node-manager-invariant: r1 [Should-fix] §4.9 Observation bullet; Key abstractions observe::classify, r1 [Should-fix] §4.9 'An observed move of its pane or tab (outside a plan) is not adopted as its placement; reconciliation restores the recorded tab.', r1 [Nit] §4.7 'Target must exist and be live'; §4.8 first-seat assignment; §4.9 reopen 'for an active seat' | rule: §4.9 states one invariant: "the node manager seat and its teamspace are Active, and only a plan can change its recorded placement". Every entry path is then checked against it, and only behaviour with an existing mechanism is promised. node-manager set and first-seat assignment require an Active target (or activate it as a listed effect). The observe::classify workspace and tab cascade drops the node manager's teamspace from `retire`, not only its seat and clones, and the spec states what happens to that teamspace's other seats. An observed out-of-plan move is tolerated and surfaced (moved_out plus a warning), because no move-back primitive exists, and reopening is promised only for closure. Audit the other cascade paths (TemplateEdit, ApplicationRetire, undo compensation) against the same invariant.
+- Independent (local, no cluster): r1 [Nit] §4.3 integrity suffix; §4.5 step 6; §4.6 'if S is the node manager → None' (caller-aware suffix: if the caller is the node manager, use the "report it to the user" form); r1 [Nit] §4.11 'inside do_retire_seat ... compute the retiring seat's effective manager M'; Key abstractions model::manager Errors (choose one disposition for an Integrity error during observed-cascade reparenting).
